  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...No hazardous weather expected through early next \nweek. \n\nA cold front is moving through the area early this morning. A\nfew heavier showers have developed ahead of the front, though\nthese weakened within the hour. Otherwise, just seeing drizzle\nto light rain. Rain moves east of the area by around sunrise,\nthen dry and sunnier conditions prevail today.  \n\nHigh pressure settles over the region Friday, the slides\noffshore over the weekend. Dry conditions and seasonable \ntemperatures are expected. A series of upper level low pressure\nsystems pass nearby. The northern stream upper level low will \ndrop a reinforcing (and dry) cold front through region early on\nSaturday, delivering extra cloud cover. Expect highs in the 70s\n(60s mountains) through Tuesday and  overnight lows in the 40s \nand 50s. Upper level ridging persists through the middle of \nnext week with a gradual warming trend expected.",
